rt's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049091} :encompassing/weight 0.5}] :topic/id #uuid "91edf602-4db5-5995-a70e-acdee225f178" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087717 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087518 :question/id #uuid "53ce2176-ae44-578d-8fba-35c5018d4162" :question/math-academy-id "e-5075" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=3t, \\,\\,\\, y=t^3, \\quad -3\\leq t \\leq 3,\n$$\n\nfill in the following table of values.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n" :question/worked-solution "First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=3t.$ This gives\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nNow, we work out the $y$-values using $y=t^3.$ This gives\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-27$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$27$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf50e27-a8c3-52e7-be21-5d7ed61e5512" :knowledge-point/title "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087721 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087522 :question/id #uuid "b322617c-ab21-5ce8-997f-2f10813b4280" :question/math-academy-id "e-5098" :question/problem "Plot the graph of the parametrically defined curve\n\n$$\nx=t(t-6), \\,\\,\\, y=t^3, \\quad -2\\leq t \\leq 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t(t-6).$ This gives\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t^3.$ This gives\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$16$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/f1/f15f25af0c4804dc811a0ab231ba2ef3ecce2ecd12501a1f2d8b9e34b71a505b.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Curve Defined Parametrically"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087722 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087523 :question/id #uuid "a792fa16-e1fd-5f30-a128-bbc49a285429" :question/math-academy-id "e-5099" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^2-6t, \\,\\,\\, y=t^4+4, \\quad t \\in (-\\infty , \\infty),\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2}-6t \\\\  & ={(t-3)}^{2}-(3)^{2} \\\\  & ={(t-3)}^{2}-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\left( t-3\\right)^2 \\geq 0,$ we can conclude that $x \\geq -9.$\n\n- To find the range of $y=t^4+4,$ notice that $t^4 \\geq 0,$ and consequently $y \\geq 4.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x \\geq -9$ and $y \\geq 4.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087736 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087542 :question/id #uuid "25ab094c-a35e-5507-a6df-459361ff6fcd" :question/math-academy-id "e-5292" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx = 4\\cos\\theta, \\,\\,\\, y = 2\\sin\\theta, \\quad 0\\leq \\theta <     2\\pi,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\leq\\theta <  2\\pi,$ we have $-1 \\leq \\cos{\\theta} \\leq 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -4 & \\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 4 \\\\ -4 & \\le x\\le 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-4 \\leq x \\leq 4.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\leq\\theta <  2\\pi,$ we have $-1 \\leq \\sin{\\theta} \\leq 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -2 & \\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 2 \\\\ -2 & \\le y\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-2 \\leq y \\leq 2.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $-4 \\leq x \\leq 4$ and $-2 \\leq y \\leq 2.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation Defined in Terms of Trigonometric Functions"}] :topic/math-academy-id 803 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048259} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048689} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049144} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049231} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049485} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050171} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050227} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050531}] :topic/title "Graphing Curves Defined Parametrically"}]}
